# Normalise line endings.
#
# Without this, Windows checks out CRLF and Linux checks out LF, so the same
# file has different bytes on different machines and every diff is noise. This
# code is edited on Windows and RUNS on the UNO Q's Debian side, so it crosses
# that boundary constantly.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repository and checks out LF everywhere.
# VS Code, Python and the Arduino toolchain all handle LF on Windows without
# complaint.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats git must never try to normalise.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.eim  binary
